PHASE 12 — VALIDATION RULE
✅ STEP 12: Create the Validation Rule (Reopen After 7 Days)
This rule blocks saving a "Reopen Case" if the original case was closed less than 7 days ago. It shows an error message to the admin.
Navigate to Validation Rules:
1.	Setup → Object Manager → Case
2.	On the left, click Validation Rules
3.	Click New
Fill in the Validation Rule:
Field	Value
Rule Name	Reopen_After_7_Days
Active	✅ Check this box
Description	Prevents reopening a case that was closed less than 7 days ago

The Formula:
In the "Error Condition Formula" text box, paste this exactly:
AND(
  RecordType.DeveloperName = "Reopen_Case",
  NOT(ISBLANK(Reopen_Form__c)),
  NOT(ISBLANK(Reopen_Form__r.ClosedDate)),
  (TODAY() - DATEVALUE(Reopen_Form__r.ClosedDate)) < 7
)
What this formula does (plain English):
•	RecordType.DeveloperName = "Reopen_Case" → Only applies when admin chose "Reopen Case" record type
•	NOT(ISBLANK(Reopen_Form__c)) → Checks that the lookup field is actually filled out
•	NOT(ISBLANK(Reopen_Form__r.ClosedDate)) → Goes and looks at the original case and checks if it has a close date
•	(TODAY() - DATEVALUE(Reopen_Form__r.ClosedDate)) < 7 → Compares today's date to the original case's close date

To check your formula is correct, click the "Check Syntax" button below the formula box. It should say: "No Syntax Errors"

Error Message:
Field	Value
Error Message	This case cannot be reopened yet. Please wait at least 7 days after the case was closed before submitting a reopen request.
Error Location	Top of Page

Click Save
✅ Validation Rule created!

